  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 213 PM EDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\n- Greater chances of rain, mainly this afternoon\n\nBased on radar and satellite trends, combined with model \nguidance, have raised PoPs to near categorical this afternoon. \nThunderstorms are not expected but there should be a fairly \nextensive coverage of measurable precipitation. Rain should be \nmostly, if not totally, out of the forecast area by this evening.\n\nAs noted before, winds should decrease rapidly this evening as the \nsurface high moves into Lower MI. We are still looking at lows in \nthe 40s Monday morning with upper 30s not out of the question in the \nfavorably cooler sandy soil regions to the north.\n\n\n- Showers, thunderstorms, possible heavy rain starts Tuesday\n\nA cyclonically breaking upper shortwave trough originating from the \nnorthern Rockies with a surface low tracking into Canada by Tuesday. \nThis will amplify the downstream upper ridge and push it eastward \nacross the Great Lakes. The associated eastward progression of the \nsurface high will introduce increasing southerly flow in its wake. \nThe cold front an associated low level theta-e ridging will enter \nthe forecast area early Tuesday morning. With MUCAPE approaching \n1000 J/kg, there will be a chance for thunderstorms.\n\nAs noted previously, the cold front is expected to stall somewhere \nin the vicinity of the southern CWA. There will be a sharp theta-e \nand conditional instability gradient with this feature. ECMWF ensemble\n(ECE) mean guidance indicates precipitable water values approaching\n2 inches, which is highly anomalous with respect to both climatology\nfor this time of year and with respect to the propensity of the ECE\nto forecast values this high for this time of year. WPC is indicating\na marginal risk for excessive rainfall, which is quite reasonable.\nHowever, accurate placement of the actual threat area will be tricky\nand highly location-dependent given the sharpness of the boundary.\n\n\n- Unsettled into this weekend\n\nEnsemble guidance really speaks to the poor predictability leading \ninto this weekend. Often it's possible to carve out a particular day \nthat's likely to be dry. Not so this time. While there is a signal \nfor a dry day happening at some point, which day that is has varied\nfrom run to run. Hence, we are featuring persistent 20-40 percent\nPoPs through the period.",
